WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:02.972
My name is Ashe.
我的名字叫阿什。

00:00:02.972 --> 00:00:05.106
I'm from Houston, Texas.
我来自得克萨斯州休斯敦。

00:00:05.106 --> 00:00:08.839
How I met your mother means comfort to me.
《老爸老妈浪漫史》对我来说意味着慰藉。

00:00:08.839 --> 00:00:15.507
2009 I lost my very young mom, 37 years old, to a very rare form of cancer.
2009年，我因一种非常罕见的癌症失去了我年轻的母亲，她当时只有37岁。

00:00:15.507 --> 00:00:19.863
And in turn I lost everyone that I called family.
随之我也失去了所有我称之为家人的人。

00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:26.442
So 20 year old me, very lost, very confused, and very alone had this show.
所以20岁的我，非常迷茫、非常困惑、也非常孤独，却有这部剧陪着。

00:00:26.442 --> 00:00:31.510
Being able to connect with characters and feel a comfort.
能够与角色产生共鸣并感受到一种慰藉，

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:38.350
that I hadn't felt since my mom had been around, meant so much to me and really did help me grow as a person.
这种自我母亲去世后再也没有感受过的慰藉，对我的意义极其重大，并且确实帮助了我作为个人的成长。

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.990
I've carried this show with me throughout my adulthood.
这部剧一直伴随着我度过了整个成年期。

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:45.950
Now I am 36 and it really means a lot.
现在我36岁了，它真的意义非凡。

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:57.350
I actually got a chance to see one of Josh's shows in Houston a few years back, which was also very comforting and brought that same feeling back.
几年前，我甚至有机会在休斯敦观看了乔伊的其中一场演出，那同样非常温馨，把那种感觉又带回来了。

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:02.590
I'm so grateful that you're doing this podcast and I am entirely grateful for how I met your mother.
我非常感激你们在做这个播客，我也由衷地感激《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:08.819
I'm alone, all be soon.
我孤身一人，很快就会团聚。

00:01:08.819 --> 00:01:14.980
You're New York City, when I see you.
纽约城啊，当我看到你。

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:21.060
Please permit me to tell you everything in New York City.
请允许我对你倾诉在纽约城的一切。

00:01:22.959 --> 00:01:29.120
Well, hello out there listeners and watchers and fans of how I met your mother.
那么，收听、收看以及喜爱《老爸老妈浪漫史》的朋友们、听众们、粉丝们，大家好。

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.840
Welcome to How We Made Your Mother, I'm Josh Radner.
欢迎来到《我们是如何创造老爸老妈浪漫史的》，我是乔什·拉德纳。

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.000
I played Ted Mosby for nine seasons on How I Met Your Mother.
我在《老爸老妈浪漫史》中饰演了九季的泰德·莫斯比。

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.340
I am joined by my friend Craig Thomas who co-created the show with Carter Bays.
和我一起的是我的朋友克雷格·托马斯，他与卡特·贝斯共同创作了这部剧。

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.260
Hi Craig.
嗨，克雷格。

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:43.500
Hey Josh.
嗨，乔什。

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.340
How's it going?
最近怎么样？

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:48.159
I, every time Alec, you make me cry with these openings of the show.
艾利克，每次你用这些开场白，都让我感动得想哭。

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:49.840
What a beautiful story.
多美的一个故事啊。

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.159
What a beautiful story.
多美的一个故事啊。

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:52.000
Thank you, Ash.
谢谢你，阿什。

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.239
Thank you for sharing that with us.
谢谢你与我们分享这些。

00:01:53.239 --> 00:02:00.000
I think when you're in, when you're in grief and something makes you laugh or someone makes you laugh, you almost always forget it.
我想，当你处于悲伤之中时，如果有什么事能让你笑出声，或者有人能让你笑，你几乎永远都不会忘记。

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.259
There's something about the, so anything that can, I don't know, alleviate a kind of heavy moment with some lightheartedness.
某种程度上……因此，任何能用轻松愉快的心情来缓解这种沉重时刻的事情，

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:11.520
You feel grateful and loyal to that thing forever.
都会让你永远对它心怀感激和忠诚。

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.360
That sounds like what we were able to provide for her.
听起来这就是我们能够为她提供的东西。

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.800
Yeah, it's amazing.
是的，这太惊人了。

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:20.840
I mean, I can't imagine how hard that was to at such a young age to go through that.
我的意思是，我无法想象在那么年轻的时候经历这些有多么艰难。

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.960
If the show provided comfort, it's amazing.
如果这部剧能提供慰藉，那真是太棒了。

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:28.520
It's amazing that seems like she's almost the age now that her mother was, if I was tracking that correctly.
太惊人了，如果我没记错的话，她现在几乎和她母亲当年去世时的年龄一样大。

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:35.080
So for the show to have meant that to her, and now she's an adult and at that age, and like that it's still part of her life, Thank you so much today.
所以，这部剧对她曾有这样的意义，而现在她长大了，到了那个年纪，它仍然是她生活的一部分，今天非常感谢你。

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:43.039
That is very much was our greatest hope in making this show that it would reach somebody like you Ash and at the moment you needed it.
这正是我们制作这部剧时最大的期望，希望它能触动像你这样的人，阿什，就在你最需要它的时候。

00:02:43.039 --> 00:02:44.599
Thank you for letting us know that.
谢谢你让我们知道这一切。

00:02:44.599 --> 00:02:46.759
I mean, that is the greatest gift just to know that.
我的意思是，知道这些就是最棒的礼物。

